.TH "YAMLR-SCAN" "1" "March 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBLocal Analysis & Read-Only Audit\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr scan\fR command is the core auditing engine. It performs three layers of analysis \fB100% locally\fR:
.PP
1.  \fBSyntax & Structure\fR: Checks for valid YAML and basic Kubernetes fields.
.PP
2.  \fBSchema Validation\fR: Validates against K8s API schemas (strict typing).
.PP
37.  \fBPolicy Enforcement (OPA)\fR: Runs custom Rego policies.
.PP
8.  \fBScientific Benchmarking\fR: via the \fBaudit\fR alias, measure healing accuracy (HAS).
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# Basic Audit
yamlr scan .

# Audit a specific target K8s version
yamlr scan . --kube-version 1.31

# CI/CD Gate: Fail if any errors found
yamlr scan . --fail-on error

# Ultra-Scale: Stream results to NDJSON for 10k+ files
yamlr scan . --stream-to audit_log.ndjson
.RE
.fi
.SH "ADVANCED FEATURES"
.SS "1. Identity Mode (`--identity-mode`)"
Yamlr uses AI-like heuristics ("Brain") to identify resources even if \fBapiVersion\fR or \fBkind\fR is missing. You can control this behavior:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--identity-mode=infer\fR (Default): Attempts to identify broken resources (e.g., "This looks like a Service").
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--identity-mode=strict\fR: Skips any file that doesn't strictly declare \fBapiVersion\fR and \fBkind\fR. Useful for reducing noise in large repos.
.SS "2. OPA Policy Engine (`--opa-bundle`)"
Yamlr embeds a full Open Policy Agent engine. You can feed it existing policies:
.PP
.nf
.RS
# Use a remote bundle
yamlr scan . --opa-bundle https://policies.mycorp.com/bundle.tar.gz

# Use local Gatekeeper ConstraintTemplates
yamlr scan . --opa-bundle ./gatekeeper/templates/
.RE
.fi
\fINote: Yamlr automatically detects if the input is a raw Rego file, a tarball bundle, or a Kubernetes ConstraintTemplate.\fR
.PP
.SS "3. Output Formats (`--output`)"
Integrate with other tools using structured output.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--output=text\fR (Default): Human-readable table.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--output=json\fR: Full structured report.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--output=sarif\fR: **GitHub Security** format. Upload directly to GitHub Code Scanning.
.nf
.RS
# CI/CD Example
yamlr scan . --output sarif > yamlr.sarif
.RE
.fi
.SS "4. Epic 21 Compliance (Enterprise)"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--evidence-dir <DIR>\fR: Directory to store generated cryptographic DNA evidence receipts natively.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--adapters-dir <DIR>\fR: Directory to dynamically load and execute custom Python/Bash remediation scripts natively against the AST.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--kyverno-report <PATH>\fR: Path to ingest a Kyverno \fBPolicyReport\fR JSON file and map its findings to Yamlr auto-fixes.
.SS "5. CI/CD & Ultra-Scale Flags"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--fail-on CHOICE\fR: Exit 1 if issues found. Choices: \fBany\fR, \fBwarning\fR, \fBerror\fR.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--stream-to FILE\fR: Stream incremental results to NDJSON (Ultra-Scale).
.SS "🛡 Universal Expert Flags"
These flags are available across almost all primary Yamlr commands:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--diff\fR**: Show visual diff of changes (Preview mode).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--dry-run\fR**: Alias for \fB--diff\fR.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fast\fR**: Skip heavy semantic analysis for maximum speed.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--kube-version <V>\fR**: Force a specific Kubernetes version (e.g., \fB1.31\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--catalog <PATH>\fR**: (Optional) Path to custom catalog. Yamlr now includes an **Embedded Magic Fallback** if this is omitted.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--max-depth <N>\fR**: Limit recursive scanning depth (Default: 10).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--ext <list>\fR**: Comma-separated list of file extensions (Default: \fB.yaml,.yml\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--concurrency <N>\fR**: Number of parallel worker processes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--strict\fR**: Treat all schema warnings as hard errors.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--compact\fR**: Use minimal whitespace (2-space indent) in output.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--health-threshold <0-100>\fR**: Minimum score to pass (Default: 70).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--namespace <name>\fR**: Default namespace for generated resources.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--check-deprecations\fR**: Audit for and record deprecated K8s APIs.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--cpu-limit <limit>\fR**: Default CPU for auto-injection (e.g., \fB500m\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--mem-limit <limit>\fR**: Default Memory for auto-injection (e.g., \fB512Mi\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-limits\fR**: Auto-inject missing CPU/Memory limits.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-probes\fR**: Auto-inject missing Liveness/Readiness probes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-namespace\fR**: Auto-inject default namespace if missing.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fix-tags\fR**: Auto-remediate \fB:latest\fR or missing image tags.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--harden\fR**: Apply security hardening (Non-root, Read-only FS).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--stream-to <FILE>\fR**: Batch-mode: Stream results to NDJSON (prevents RAM saturation).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fail-on <CHOICE>\fR**: Exit 1 if specified severity found (error/warning/any).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--summary-only\fR**: Show aggregate stats only (recommended for 100+ files).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--plain\fR**: ASCII-only output mode (Recommended for Log redirection).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--verbose\fR**: Show full audit logs and engine stages.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR**: Minimal output mode (CI/CD optimized; errors and exit codes only).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--identity-mode {infer,strict}\fR**: Control how Yamlr identifies resources (Default: infer).
